    {
      "turn": 1,
      "doctor_question": "Hello, I’m glad you came in. What brings you in today?",
      "targeted_symptom": "S005",
      "patient_response": "Hi, doctor. Well, what brings me in is... I just cannot seem to keep my work in order anymore. I work down at the dry cleaners, and lately, my counter is just a complete disaster. I’ve got claim tickets, receipts, workshop notes, and customer jobs all piled together in this huge mountain until I honestly do not know what to handle first. \n\nSpeaking of customers, Mrs. Higgins came in yesterday with this beautiful vintage silk blouse—it had a massive red wine stain right on the collar. I told her, \"Mrs. Higgins, you know club soda is a myth, you should have brought it straight to me!\" But she insisted on trying to scrub it out herself first at her dinner party, which just ruins the fibers, you know? Silk is so incredibly delicate. My sister actually gave me a lovely silk scarf for my 50th birthday a few years ago, but I’m terrified to wear it because I always end up spilling my morning coffee on myself. I buy the dark roast from that little cafe next door to the shop, the one with the green awning? They make a great cup, but the lids never stay on tight. \n\nWait, what was I saying? Oh, right, the piles at work. Yeah, the receipts and the tickets. I just... I look at it all and I don't even know where to start anymore.",
