    {
      "turn": 4,
      "doctor_question": "Do you often feel restless or like you have to move around a lot when you’re supposed to stay still?",
      "targeted_symptom": "S011",
      "patient_response": "Oh, absolutely. I just cannot stay glued to a chair for long. Like, whenever we have those church committee meetings, or even the fabric-care trainings at work, I keep finding reasons to get up. I'll get up for a glass of water, or to grab some papers, or just to check on something in the back. Everybody else is sitting perfectly still, and I'm just up and down, up and down. \n\nSpeaking of the church committee, we're planning the spring bake sale right now, and let me tell you, trying to organize the sign-up sheet is a nightmare. Mildred always insists on bringing her fruitcake, but nobody buys fruitcake in April! I tried to tell her she should make her lemon bars instead, they are just divine. She uses fresh lemon juice, not that bottled stuff. I bought the bottled stuff once when I was making a marinade for chicken, and it just tasted so metallic, you know? I was making chicken piccata, which my husband usually loves, but that time it was just... off. We ended up ordering a pizza instead. We get it from that place on the corner with the brick oven, they do this amazing thin crust with extra mushrooms... \n\nWait, what was the question? Oh, staying still. Yes, I'm always having to get up and move around when I'm supposed to be sitting.",
